// 3. EVENTS CARRY VALUES
//
// Each event is a bag of named values. sound() sets which instrument.
// note() sets pitch. Everything chained after adds more to the bag,
// and the synth reads the whole bag when the event fires.

note("c3 eb3 g3 bb3 ~ g3")
  .sound("sine")   // which oscillator
  .cutoff(500)         // low-pass filter, in Hz. the big one for character
  .decay(1.5)          // how fast it falls away
  .sustain(0)          // 0 means it never holds, so it plucks
  .gain(0.8)
  .delay(0.3)           // level

// Press tab after typing a dot to see what else exists. Each entry shows
// what it does and a sensible range, which saves guessing.
//
// The filter is the single most useful knob here. Try cutoff(300),
// then cutoff(3000), and listen to how much of the character it owns.
